Reason for all three skips: RAILWAY_TEST_JDBC_URL, RAILWAY_TEST_DB_USER, and RAILWAY_TEST_DB_PASSWORD were not set. JDBC behavior is SKIPPED, not PASS. The same three variables were absent when checked while finalizing this log; no JDBC test was run against PostgreSQL.

Sheet criteria and focused evidence
- "Each Node applies in the same order": fiveNodesApplyTheSameOrderAndLaggingNodesStayPrefixes. This uses five independent in-memory RaftState/applier/repository fixtures in one JVM. It is not five running Node processes, TCP replication, or a majority-commit test.
- "Crash/replay does not sell twice": restartReplayDoesNotSellTwice and crashBetweenSinkSuccessAndMarkAppliedDoesNotSellTwice. Replay preserves repository checkpoint, tickets, seats, and business event count; the replayed NO_OP reports no business outcome.
- "NO_OP does not create business event": noOpAdvancesPersistentCheckpointWithoutBusinessEvent.
- Additional covered behavior: transientStorageFailureRetriesSameIndexAndNeverSkipsLaterEntries; fatalDecodeFailureLatchesAndStopsWithoutThrowing; durableIndexHoleIsFatalAndFailsClosed; lyingCallbackCannotApplyBeyondCommitIndex; repeatedAndNestedCallsAreIgnored; appliedHookFailureIsSwallowedAndDoesNotLatchFatalFailure.

Limitations
- The in-memory tests use fakes/fixtures. The follower test uses PersistentRaftNode with a simulated leader request in-process; this does not prove communication over real TCP.
- The five-node test is five independent in-memory states within one JVM, not five real nodes and not evidence of Raft majority commit.
- PostgreSQL-backed D18 tests were skipped as noted above; no claim of JDBC verification is made.
- The applier's defensive catch for state.entryAt(index) failure has no direct test. A legal RaftState cannot be created with commitIndex beyond lastLogIndex: advanceCommitIndex rejects it; truncateSuffixFrom refuses to truncate committed entries; restore validates contiguous log entries and lastApplied within the log. RaftState was not modified to manufacture an invalid state.

