Conclusions / unresolved ownership
- No call appending a NO_OP during becomeLeader was found. The RaftLogEntry.noOp factory exists, but the search shows no production use on the leader transition path.
- BookingRaftBridge (TV2-D17) is absent from origin/main.
- Runtime wiring remains open: identify the owner to connect the applier to PersistentRaftNode and the Leader's post-CommitAdvancer path.
- Assign production RaftLogEntry-to-BookingCommand decoder ownership to TV2/TV3; do not create a second codec in D18.
- Identify the runtime caller/owner for CommitAdvancer.advance().

TV2/TV6 handoff
On replay, CommittedCommandApplier can return the prior BusinessResult to hooks.onApplied even though it does not apply the business operation again. This is a redelivery, not a new business event. The layer delivering a Client response must be idempotent and must not emit a duplicate CONFIRMED as a new event.

Change scope
- Only this evidence log is updated in this fix.
- No source, test, or raw Maven log was changed.
- JDBC remains unverified (SKIPPED). No real TCP, five-process cluster, or quorum commit was tested.
